WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.180
I'll leave Sakurada, forget about my ability,
and live out the rest of my life.

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:06.140
It'll just be a week, though.

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:09.690
Do you want to know your own future?

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:10.990
Yes.

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:15.110
Even if it's something painful?

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:16.690
Yes, please.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:23.250
You're going to be involved in something big...

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:26.630
Something involving my successor.

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:29.380
Does such a person exist?

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:32.180
The Bureau has been looking
for one for a long time now.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:37.140
But no matter how much they looked, they couldn't
find anyone with the ability to see the future.

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:39.260
However,

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:42.820
you know someone who does possess it.

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:45.570
You've met that person a little over two years ago.

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:48.250
Is your successor...

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:51.200
Is the future-seeing ability user a girl?

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.110
Yes.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:57.780
A slender girl with short hair, big eyes,
and about the age of a middle schooler.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:00:59.030
Yes.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:06.290
Is it the girl who died two years ago?

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:11.690
Correct. And you will run into her again.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:18.850
Two Years Earlier

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:38.870
<i>It's been two weeks since
the second semester started.</i>

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:42.260
<i>As well as two weeks since
Souma Sumire left this world.</i>

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:45.390
<i>She won't be coming to this rooftop anymore.</i>

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:22.300
<i>I also stopped spending time on the rooftop.</i>

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:25.560
<i>I always end up getting cold
feet when I reach the door.</i>

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:28.930
<i>I don't get any opportunities to meet
Haruki Misora anymore, either.</i>

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:32.520
<i>The last time I saw her was about a week ago.</i>

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.230
<i>We were summoned to the staff room</i>

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:36.730
<i>and encouraged to join the Service Club.</i>

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:39.280
<i>I haven't seen her since
we submitted our applications.</i>

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:44.160
<i>Or, to be more precise, I've been avoiding her.</i>

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.330
<i>When I'm sad, it rubs off on her.</i>

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:51.370
<i>I don't want to see her until
I can smile like nothing's wrong.</i>

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:54.710
<i>But it's been two weeks already.</i>

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:57.380
<i>It's a good time to change how things stand.</i>

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:03.130
A young boy hurt a girl he was
friends with using his ability.

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:07.970
It seems he doesn't understand
quite how it works yet.

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:13.730
I'd like you to use Haruki's reset to put
the world back to before he hurt her.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:19.150
And then after that, report the whole story
to me using your absolute memory.

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:21.610
The Bureau will take things from there.

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:22.950
I understand.

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:24.110
Where is Haruki?

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:26.870
I don't think her homeroom's been let out yet.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:28.120
Or so I'd assume.

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:31.370
I see. I'll fill her in later, then.

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:33.920
It's your first task in the Service Club.

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:35.000
Good luck.

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:48.350
Kei, I can't use my reset ability.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:51.180
You mean to say you don't have a save?

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:54.600
No, I saved around 5 p.m. two days ago.

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:57.650
What's stopping you, then?

00:04:57.650 --> 00:04:58.940
I don't know.

00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:01.530
I just get the feeling I wouldn't be able to.

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:08.990
Why don't you sit down for now?

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:10.740
Should I?

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:12.120
I'm not forcing you.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:13.500
You should do what you want to do.

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:30.720
Haruki is changing.

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:34.180
She'll be feeling a lot of things from now on.

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:36.480
She'll learn them from you.

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:42.110
You were able to save two days ago, right?

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:42.940
Yes.

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:44.530
I believe I was.

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:45.650
How can you be so sure?

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:48.160
I don't have any qualms about saving.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:51.530
But I don't feel like I can reset in the first place.

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:53.450
What's the difference between them?

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:57.920
You ordered me to save.

00:05:58.170 --> 00:05:59.080
Did I?

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:00.170
Yes.

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:02.800
You told me to save once every three days.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:07.630
Kei, give me the order to reset.

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:11.550
I feel like I can do it if you tell me to.

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:18.560
<i>Why won't you order me to reset?</i>

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:23.150
<i>Thinking ahead, it'd be best
if you're able to reset on your own.</i>

00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:27.400
<i>If you absolutely need my orders,
it might pose a big obstacle sometime in the future.</i>

00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:31.820
<i>I was sure he'd just tell me to reset right away.</i>

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:34.200
<i>Has he come to hate my ability?</i>

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:37.080
<i>I can easily see that being the case.</i>

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:43.420
<i>My reset most likely had something
to do with Souma Sumire's death.</i>

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:47.170
<i>Kei has been avoiding me ever since she died.</i>

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:49.970
<i>Even though he'd wanted my ability so much before.</i>

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:53.970
<i>Even though I'd decided I'd use it for him.</i>

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:58.640
<i>Now I understand.</i>

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:03.150
<i>You can't use Sakurada's abilities
unless you truly want to.</i>

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:06.360
<i>I decided to follow Asai Kei,</i>

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:09.860
<i>but he no longer wishes for
me to use my reset ability.</i>

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:12.870
<i>Not acting in accordance with his
wishes is the wrong thing to do.</i>

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:16.870
<i>I'm sure that's what I assumed
somewhere deep in my mind.</i>

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:20.210
<i>That's why I can't reset anymore.</i>

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:26.550
<i>Souma Sumire died as a result of a reset.</i>

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:30.090
<i>She was alive in the previous timeline,</i>

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:32.680
<i>but she died in the current one.</i>

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:34.850
<i>I've taken the ability to reset too lightly.</i>

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:40.390
<i>For the most part, everything went the
same way as it did before whenever we reset.</i>

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:43.400
<i>The contents of the newspaper never changed.</i>

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:46.820
<i>Neither did the results of sport matches
nor changes in the stock market.</i>

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:50.490
<i>The same accidents in faraway cities
would happen again as well.</i>

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:54.160
<i>That led me to believe that the future
doesn't change just because we reset.</i>

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:59.620
<i>I'd figured the only exception was me
retaining my memories from before the reset.</i>

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:02.830
<i>But Souma Sumire died,</i>

00:08:02.830 --> 00:08:04.630
<i>and I had nothing to do with it.</i>

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:06.710
<i>I don't know why she did,</i>

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:10.720
<i>but it means unforeseen accidents
are not out of the equation.</i>

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:16.010
<i>That's why I couldn't tell her to reset.</i>

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:19.390
<i>Is resetting the right thing to do?</i>

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:23.140
<i>Kei probably can't come to terms with it.</i>

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:27.150
<i>But I'm sure tomorrow he'll tell me
to reset like nothing ever happened.</i>

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:31.400
<i>That way, we can carry out
our tasks in the Service Club.</i>

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:33.780
<i>We can help someone.</i>

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:37.910
<i>For that reason alone,
Kei will eventually choose to reset.</i>

00:08:39.160 --> 00:08:42.660
<i>And that means resetting is the right thing to do.</i>

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:44.670
Reset.

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:57.180
<i>It seems I was right.
Something deep within me doesn't want to reset.</i>

00:08:57.850 --> 00:09:01.930
<i>It's probably those things called
"emotions" getting in the way.</i>

00:09:09.770 --> 00:09:15.740
Every time I look at you,
it makes me think of two identical white boxes.

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:21.330
You're facing two white boxes in a white room.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:24.120
You have to open one of them,

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:26.830
but you don't know which is the right one.

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:28.380
I don't understand.

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:33.960
I'm basically saying that's how
uniform the world is to you.

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:38.010
If they were different colors,
you could pick the one you like more.

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:41.760
If they were different shapes,
you could even pick based on that.

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:45.430
But the only thing that's ever in front of you

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:49.230
are two completely identical white boxes.

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:52.730
<i>That's what Souma Sumire said.</i>

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:55.150
<i>But that isn't the case right now.</i>

00:09:55.150 --> 00:10:01.030
<i>I see resetting and not resetting
as two very different choices.</i>

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:02.490
<i>There's an obvious distinction.</i>

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:06.540
<i>The logical choice would be to reset.</i>

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:08.080
<i>Kei would choose that too.</i>

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:11.340
<i>But my emotions are getting in the way.</i>

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:13.000
<i>Kei also hates the ability.</i>

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:19.930
Reset.

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:29.020
I...

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:32.610
<i>I'm scared of Kei hating me.</i>

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:41.450
I'm from the Bureau.

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:42.950
How did it go?

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:48.210
The Bureau determined that Souma Sumire's death
was an accident unrelated to any abilities.

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:49.080
Why?

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:53.840
The connection between her death
and Haruki Misora's ability isn't clear.

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:55.590
It should be.

00:10:55.590 --> 00:10:58.050
She was alive before the reset.

00:10:58.050 --> 00:11:00.800
You're the only one claiming that.

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:04.180
Are you saying that I lied to you?

00:11:04.180 --> 00:11:07.680
The Bureau determined that
we can't rule out that possibility.

00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:12.610
Shouldn't you be able to investigate
if I'm telling the truth?

00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:15.150
I cannot answer that.

00:11:18.440 --> 00:11:22.780
If I'm able to prove that I am,

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:24.370
will you save Souma?

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:25.580
No.

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:28.660
I'm sorry, I didn't make it clear.

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:33.880
Even if what you're saying is the truth,
the Bureau won't get involved in this.

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:39.010
It's been determined Souma Sumire's death
happened separate from the usage of any abilities.

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:40.380
I see.

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:43.470
Please tell me one last thing.

00:11:44.510 --> 00:11:47.970
If the Bureau put their resources into it,

00:11:47.970 --> 00:11:52.690
would they be able to bring Souma Sumire,
someone who died two weeks ago, back to life?

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:55.110
I cannot answer that.

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:58.360
If you're an organization that
oversees the abilities in Sakurada,

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:01.200
wouldn't you know of an ability that can save her?

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:04.160
I cannot answer that.

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:09.410
Reset.

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:14.830
Reset. Reset.

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:53.960
Are you crying?

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:01.960
Hey. What are you doing here?

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:04.590
I came here to see the sunset.

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:06.840
That so? Why, though?

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:09.850
No reason, really. I just kinda felt like it.

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:10.720
I see.

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:13.730
Want a Kit Kat?

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:18.230
Yeah, sure.

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:22.360
Here.

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:23.650
Thank you.

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:32.830
Did you know that a girl died around here?

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:36.420
Yeah, I did. She went to my school.

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:38.330
Really? What was her name?

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:41.500
Souma Sumire.

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:43.420
How do you spell that?

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:47.760
"Souma" spelled S-O-U-M-A,
and "Sumire" spelled S-U-M-I-R-E.

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:49.680
Put it all together and you get "Souma Sumire."

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:52.260
I can tell you were pretty close.

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:53.020
Your girlfriend, maybe?

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:55.270
No, why would you think that?

00:13:55.270 --> 00:14:00.360
Most people wouldn't remember someone's full
name just because they went to the same school.

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:05.030
And being able to effortlessly spell her name
like that tells me you were more than just friends.

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:08.160
I just happen to have an ability like that.

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:09.660
Like what?

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:11.990
I can remember anything and everything.

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:13.160
Oh yeah?

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:15.450
So what brings you here?

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:18.790
A girl slipped and fell into the river.

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:21.130
If it's dangerous here, it should be made safer.

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:23.550
Made safer? Do you want to put up
some kind of railing or something?

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:25.670
That's what I had in mind.

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:29.470
To steal your words: I have an ability like that.

00:14:29.470 --> 00:14:31.680
What kind of ability?

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:34.680
I can build fences in just a few minutes.

00:14:34.680 --> 00:14:36.600
You build fences?

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:40.600
I can also tear up clouds
and make a hole in the moon.

00:14:41.270 --> 00:14:44.110
Not that I've ever done that,
but I think I'd be able to.

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:48.110
You're not making any sense.

00:14:48.110 --> 00:14:50.240
I don't expect you to understand.

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:51.990
Want some Koala March?

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:53.870
No, thank you.

00:14:54.990 --> 00:14:56.370
But they're so good!

00:14:56.370 --> 00:14:59.830
If I eat too much, I won't have any room for dinner.

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:00.500
Right.

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:02.460
I'll eat them all by myself, then.

00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:11.930
I wanted to put railings in dangerous places.

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:13.760
But you know...

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:17.890
I climbed all the way to the top and
couldn't find any place dangerous enough.

00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:19.890
Then I found you.

00:15:19.890 --> 00:15:23.940
And that made me wonder if the girl
who died here actually committed suicide.

00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:25.690
That came out of nowhere.

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:29.240
How is me being here at all related to Souma?

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:32.070
You just kinda looked like you were ready to die.

00:15:32.570 --> 00:15:36.160
The wind is strong, the sunset is beautiful...

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:39.830
It seemed to me like you were ready
to die for trivial reasons like that.

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:42.830
So I tried to put two and two together.

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:46.960
For whatever reasons, a girl... I mean, Souma died,

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:51.630
and knowing that, you, her boyfriend,
decided to commit suicide to follow her.

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:54.260
You couldn't be more off.

00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:55.760
Really?

00:15:55.760 --> 00:16:00.730
But everything went according to my script,
up to how you effortlessly spelled her name.

00:16:00.730 --> 00:16:04.860
For the record, what would you do
if I really were here to die?

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:06.860
I'd save you, of course.

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:09.320
That's what the Kit Kat was for.

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:13.030
Did you think a Kit Kat was going
to change my mind about dying?

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:16.530
I find it hard to believe anyone would want
to die after eating something that good.

00:16:18.410 --> 00:16:21.500
And I guess it meant "take a chill pill" too.

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:23.620
A pill in the guise of a candy bar?

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:27.250
"Have a break." That sort of meaning.

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:32.420
I'm going to head home.

00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:34.380
Thank you for the Kit Kat.

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:36.890
What's your name?

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:39.560
Asai Kei. What about you?

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:40.930
Ukawa Sasane.

00:16:42.140 --> 00:16:43.640
Want some Koala March?

00:16:47.360 --> 00:16:48.440
Reset.

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:51.940
Reset.

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:56.200
Reset.

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:05.250
I'm scared of Kei hating me.

00:17:08.340 --> 00:17:10.550
Is that phone strap some sort of memento?

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:12.920
No, not really.

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:15.930
But I really can't see you as the
type to use that kind of thing.

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:19.180
It was originally a keychain.

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:22.680
My parents were rarely ever home.

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:25.060
So when I got my own key,
my mom put this thing on them.

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:27.650
Was that before you came to Sakurada?

00:17:27.650 --> 00:17:28.440
Yeah.

00:17:28.440 --> 00:17:32.070
I threw away my house key
when I decided to live in Sakurada.

00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:35.070
Yeah, uh, that's what you call a memento.

00:17:35.070 --> 00:17:36.030
Is it?

00:17:36.030 --> 00:17:36.910
Duh.

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:40.240
<i>I threw away my key,</i>

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:43.160
<i>but what was I hoping to get in exchange?</i>

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:45.080
<i>I don't even have to think.</i>

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:48.790
<i>I'm here because I was drawn to Sakurada's abilities.</i>

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:56.130
I'm sorry, Kei.

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:59.430
I couldn't reset on my own after all.

00:17:59.890 --> 00:18:02.180
I'll give you the order, then.

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:03.390
Let's reset.

00:18:04.640 --> 00:18:05.640
Kei.

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:09.060
Are you sure you want to do this?

00:18:09.310 --> 00:18:10.610
Of course.

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:12.690
Resetting is the right thing to do now.

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:17.200
Don't you hate my ability?

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:18.860
Hate it? Why would I?

00:18:19.530 --> 00:18:22.490
A reset killed Souma Sumire.

00:18:24.240 --> 00:18:26.580
Souma Sumire died in an accident.

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:28.670
Our reset had nothing to do with it.

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:29.880
She died, and that's the end of it.

00:18:30.170 --> 00:18:34.760
Wouldn't she be still alive if we hadn't reset?

00:18:34.760 --> 00:18:36.670
That might be true.

00:18:36.670 --> 00:18:40.050
But does that really matter?

00:18:40.050 --> 00:18:44.220
If it's too dangerous an ability,
don't you think we shouldn't use it?

00:18:44.640 --> 00:18:48.350
It's true that we might change
someone's future by resetting.

00:18:48.350 --> 00:18:52.190
We might ruin someone's life
and never even know it.

00:18:52.190 --> 00:18:56.690
But at the same time,
it has an equal chance of helping someone.

00:18:56.690 --> 00:19:00.860
Let's say there's a man who
hurt himself and started bleeding.

00:19:00.860 --> 00:19:03.450
Do you think it's wrong to save him?

00:19:04.080 --> 00:19:05.080
No.

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:06.750
So that man is saved,

00:19:06.750 --> 00:19:10.460
and he goes on to eventually meet
a woman and build a happy family.

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:14.130
Do you think that's wrong?

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:15.130
No.

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:17.840
But if you hadn't saved him,

00:19:17.840 --> 00:19:20.840
the woman might've gone on to meet someone else.

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:23.640
She might have had an even happier family.

00:19:24.350 --> 00:19:27.430
The life of the child who was supposed
to be born into that family

00:19:27.430 --> 00:19:31.400
might've been indirectly
taken away by saving the man.

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:33.860
It's not limited to just abilities.

00:19:34.360 --> 00:19:38.240
Every action of every person
is constantly changing the future.

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:41.490
If you think that resetting is the only
thing interfering with the future,

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:43.120
that's nothing but conceit.

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:46.370
If you changed the future to save one person,

00:19:46.370 --> 00:19:49.790
but ended up making someone
else suffer in the process,

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:51.870
would you not feel sad?

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:54.000
Of course I would.

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:59.260
There's no better outcome than making
someone happy at no one else's expense.

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:03.010
And even then, you still want to reset?

00:20:04.390 --> 00:20:08.430
If at all possible, I'd love to be able
to create nothing but happiness.

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:10.980
In the same way that God makes miracles,

00:20:11.230 --> 00:20:14.310
I want to make people happy
without hurting anyone.

00:20:14.600 --> 00:20:17.320
But I lack the power to do that.

00:20:17.940 --> 00:20:21.280
Still, I don't want to sit by and do
nothing just because I'm powerless.

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:25.660
Even if I do hurt someone,
all I have to do is save more people than that.

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:32.410
I also think that's the right thing to do.

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:35.880
That's why I want you to help me, Haruki.

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:40.710
<i>I'm sure Kei thinks that from the bottom of his heart.</i>

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:46.550
<i>Even if all his other words
were lies to make me reset...</i>

00:20:46.970 --> 00:20:52.930
<i>Even if most of what he said were
just empty words to persuade me...</i>

00:20:52.930 --> 00:20:55.520
<i>At the very least, the last part was from his heart.</i>

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:03.150
I understand.

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:05.070
Kei, give me the order.

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:10.580
Haruki, it's time to reset.

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:13.460
Reset.

00:21:20.460 --> 00:21:23.670
<i>I did the same things as before the reset.</i>

00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:25.800
<i>I ate the same food,</i>

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:28.930
<i>read the same book,
and went to sleep at the same hour.</i>

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:33.980
<i>It's tiring to repeat what I already did once before.</i>

00:21:33.980 --> 00:21:36.810
<i>Makes me feel like I'm acting in a boring play.</i>

00:21:37.600 --> 00:21:43.490
<i>But resetting made me afraid
of changing the future unnecessarily.</i>

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:47.410
Second Time
Tuesday
September 14th

00:21:47.950 --> 00:21:49.740
Okay, I get the full story.

00:21:49.740 --> 00:21:51.790
I'll report that to the Bureau.

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:53.500
Good job.

00:21:54.250 --> 00:21:57.750
<i>And so ended our first task in the Service Club.</i>

00:21:58.210 --> 00:22:00.880
<i>The boy, who was supposed to use his ability,</i>

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:03.630
<i>and the girl, who was supposed
to get hurt because of it,</i>

00:22:03.630 --> 00:22:05.260
<i>should be safe now.</i>

00:22:05.880 --> 00:22:08.970
<i>But someone else might be
suffering because of this reset,</i>

00:22:08.970 --> 00:22:11.890
<i>and we'll never even know about it.</i>

00:22:12.390 --> 00:22:15.310
<i>I'm not sure if we did the right thing.</i>

00:22:16.480 --> 00:22:19.150
<i>What killed Souma Sumire wasn't our reset.</i>

00:22:19.440 --> 00:22:23.280
<i>It's my fault for making Haruki
reset for no real reason.</i>

00:22:23.980 --> 00:22:27.280
<i>But still, if we can save someone by doing it,</i>

00:22:28.150 --> 00:22:30.070
<i>I think we should keep using her ability.</i>

00:22:35.160 --> 00:22:37.870
<i>I was hurt because of Souma's death.</i>

00:22:37.870 --> 00:22:42.000
<i>But how I felt also hurt Haruki.</i>

00:22:42.000 --> 00:22:44.710
<i>It hurt her deeply enough to make
her unable to use her ability.</i>

00:22:44.710 --> 00:22:50.470
<i>I can think of only one way to ease her pain.</i>

00:22:51.930 --> 00:22:54.470
<i>I'll bring Souma Sumire back to life.</i>

00:22:54.890 --> 00:22:57.520
<i>I don't know if that's even possible,</i>

00:22:57.520 --> 00:23:00.350
<i>but there are countless abilities in Sakurada.</i>

00:23:00.600 --> 00:23:05.110
<i>I can't say for sure it's impossible
to bring a dead girl back to life.</i>

00:23:06.230 --> 00:23:07.030
Kei.

00:23:08.700 --> 00:23:10.280
What's wrong?

00:23:10.280 --> 00:23:11.570
We reset.

00:23:12.320 --> 00:23:14.080
I'll tell you everything now.

00:23:14.950 --> 00:23:15.740
I see.

00:23:16.370 --> 00:23:19.460
But first, there's something I want to give you.

00:23:19.910 --> 00:23:21.540
What is it?

00:23:21.540 --> 00:23:23.540
It's nothing special.

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:26.380
Next Episode

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:26.420
Reviving a dead person...
Next Episode

00:23:26.420 --> 00:23:27.710
Reviving a dead person...

00:23:27.710 --> 00:23:30.590
If you're going to bring Souma back to life,
I'll do anything to help.

00:23:30.590 --> 00:23:31.720
Is it broken?

00:23:31.720 --> 00:23:33.890
You seem happy for some reason.

00:23:33.890 --> 00:23:36.430
I think it's okay to just pray for that happiness.

00:23:36.850 --> 00:23:39.060
Hello, Kei.

00:23:40.560 --> 00:23:47.690
We're always simply standing in a rain of eternal sadness

00:23:47.690 --> 00:23:55.160
That is why I need that warmth of yours

00:23:55.780 --> 00:24:00.620
Life is but a dream we never wake up from

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:08.710
We repeat it over and over, praying for salvation

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:14.300
I kept waiting endlessly for your signal

00:24:15.260 --> 00:24:21.480
To make sure you wouldn't disappear all by yourself

00:24:22.020 --> 00:24:25.980
Ah, it doesn't matter where I am or what I'm doing

00:24:25.980 --> 00:24:29.360
My heart can't go against your will

00:24:29.360 --> 00:24:35.370
So I'd follow you even to the ends of the world

00:24:35.370 --> 00:24:42.500
I fell in love with you at the dawn of our new world

00:24:42.500 --> 00:24:49.000
But we kept pushing the hand of the clock backwards

00:24:49.000 --> 00:24:56.180
And lost not only time, but our smiles as well

00:24:56.180 --> 00:25:00.270
You're the one who brought it back

00:25:00.270 --> 00:25:07.110
And taught me that even lies can be meaningful
